Logic :

Create an empty list list to store the duplicate numbers.
Initialize i as 1 and use a while loop to place elements in their correct positions.
Check if the current element is not at its correct index (arr[i - 1] != i).
Check whether the correct position of the current element already contains the same value (arr[i - 1] != arr[arr[i - 1] - 1]).
If both conditions are true, swap the current element with the element at its correct position.
If the element is already in the correct position or a duplicate value is found, move to the next index.
Continue this process until all possible elements are placed at their correct indices.
Traverse the array again and compare each element with its expected value (index).
If an element does not match its expected value, it means that number appears more than once.
Add that duplicate number to the list.
Return the list containing all duplicate numbers.

Leetcode 442 :

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> findDuplicates(int[] arr) {
          ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        int i=1;
        while(i<=arr.length){
            if(arr[i-1]!=i && arr[i-1]!=arr[arr[i-1]-1]){
                int temp=arr[i-1];
                arr[i-1]=arr[temp-1];
                arr[temp-1]=temp;
            }
           else{
                i+=1;
            }

        }
       for(int index=1;index<=arr.length;index++){
            if(arr[index-1]!=index){
                list.add(arr[index-1]);
            }
        }
      
       
       return list;
    }
}
